UltraJSON is an ultra fast JSON encoder and decoder written in pure C
with bindings for Python. May be used as a drop in replacement for most
other JSON parsers for Python.

UltraJSON's architecture is fundamentally ill-suited to making changes
without risk of introducing new security vulnerabilities. As a result,
this library has been put into a maintenance-only mode. Support for new
Python versions will be added and critical bugs and security issues
will still be fixed but all other changes will be rejected. Users are
encouraged to migrate to orjson which is both much faster and less
likely to introduce a surprise buffer overflow vulnerability in the
future.
